---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const aspects = [
  { letter: 'S', name: 'Standards', question: 'Do executable engineering standards exist?' },
  { letter: 'C', name: 'Consumption', question: 'Are teams using them (adoption) and using them correctly (conformance)?' },
  { letter: 'A', name: 'Automation', question: 'How much is enforced automatically?' },
  { letter: 'L', name: 'Leverage', question: 'What reuse and engineering capacity do they create?' },
  { letter: 'E', name: 'Effectiveness', question: 'Did engineering and business outcomes improve?' },
]
---

<BaseLayout title="SCALE">
  <div class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8">
      <span class="text-xs font-medium px-2 py-1 bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-[var(--color-primary-dark)] rounded">PBHQ Original</span>
      <span class="text-xs font-medium px-2 py-1 bg-[var(--color-primary)]/10 text-[var(--color-primary)] rounded">Framework</span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mt-4 mb-6">SCALE</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-8">
        A machine-readable framework for telling the platform story: how engineering best
        practices are <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">S</strong>tandardized,
        <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">C</strong>onsumed,
        <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">A</strong>utomated,
        <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">L</strong>everaged, and made
        <strong class="text-[var(--color-text)]">E</strong>ffective across an organization.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-4">The Five Aspects</h2>
      <p class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-6">
        Every metric is tagged with exactly one aspect. SCALE is an aggregation and narrative
        layer over detailed maturity metrics — not another metrics catalog. Maturity frameworks
        make it cheap to generate hundreds of metrics, and cheap metrics destroy the story.
        SCALE's purpose is to make hundreds of metrics readable as five aspect-level storylines.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border-light)]">
              <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4 text-[var(--color-text)]">Letter</th>
              <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4 text-[var(--color-text)]">Aspect</th>
              <th class="text-left py-2 text-[var(--color-text)]">Question it answers</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {aspects.map((a) => (
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border-light)]">
                <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-bold text-[var(--color-primary)]">{a.letter}</td>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-[var(--color-text)]">{a.name}</td>
                <td class="py-2 text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">{a.question}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-4">Why It Matters for ProductBuilders</h2>
      <p class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mb-4">
        AI agents make it cheap to generate code and specs — they do not make it cheap to keep
        the result standardized, automated, or reused. Left unchecked, that gap is exactly how
        AI-generated systems become unmaintainable at scale: consumption outruns standards,
        automation lags enforcement, and duplicated effort erodes leverage. SCALE exists to keep
        that gap visible, aspect by aspect, so "did this actually get more maintainable" has an
        honest answer instead of a metrics dashboard nobody reads.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
        SCALE is consumed by <a href="/products/visionstudio" class="text-[var(--color-primary)] hover:underline">VisionStudio's</a>
        Maturity Model panel and is designed to sit alongside deeper assessment frameworks like
        PRISM — PRISM assesses, SCALE narrates.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 mt-10">
        <a href="https://github.com/ProductBuildersHQ/scale" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 bg-[var(--color-primary-dark)] text-white font-medium rounded-lg no-underline hover:bg-[var(--color-primary)] transition-colors">View on GitHub</a>
        <a href="/scale/" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-[var(--color-primary-dark)] font-medium rounded-lg no-underline hover:bg-[var(--color-accent-light)] transition-colors">Documentation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
